# Homework 3 - Dimension Reduction Using PCA

This assignment applies Principal Component Analysis (PCA) to a customer dataset to reduce correlated variables into a smaller number of meaningful principal components while retaining most of the original information.

## Objectives
- Load and understand the customer dataset
- Examine correlations among numerical variables
- Standardize variables using scikit-learn
- Perform Principal Component Analysis (PCA)
- Determine how many principal components should be retained
- Examine PCA loadings
- Create PCA scores for each customer
- Visualize PCA results
- Interpret the principal components from a business perspective
- Review and improve Copilot-generated code

## Analysis Includes
- Correlation matrix
- Standardized customer features
- Explained and cumulative variance
- PCA loadings
- PCA scores
- Correlation heatmap
- PCA scree plot
- Cumulative variance plot
- PC1 vs. PC2 scatterplot

## Files
- Python program for the PCA analysis
- `correlation_matrix.csv`
- `standardized_customer_features.csv`
- `pca_explained_variance.csv`
- `pca_loadings.csv`
- `pca_scores.csv`
- `correlation_heatmap.png`
- `pca_scree_plot.png`
- `pca_cumulative_variance.png`
- `pca_scatterplot.png`
- PCA analysis and business interpretation
- Copilot code-review documentation
